@@ -0,0 +1,82 @@
+# tarx
+
+A small command-line tool for listing and extracting tar archives, using only
+the Python standard library (Python 3.11+).
+
+## Usage
+
+```
+$ export PYTHONPATH=src
+
+$ python -m tarx list photos.tar.gz
+photos/a.jpg
+photos/b.jpg
+
+$ python -m tarx extract photos.tar.gz out
+extracted 2 files
+
+$ python -m tarx extract photos.tar.gz out
+python -m tarx: error: out/photos/a.jpg: already exists (use --overwrite to replace it)
+
+$ python -m tarx extract photos.tar.gz out --overwrite
+extracted 2 files
+```
+
+- `list ARCHIVE` prints every member's name, one per line, in archive order.
+- `extract ARCHIVE DEST [--overwrite]` extracts files and directories into
+  `DEST` (created if needed), keeping their relative paths and contents, then
+  prints `extracted N files` — the number of regular files written.
+
+Plain `.tar` and gzip-compressed `.tar.gz` / `.tgz` archives both work
+(`.tar.bz2` and `.tar.xz` are detected too, at no extra cost).
+
+## Exit status
+
+| Code | Meaning |
+| ---- | ------- |
+| 0 | success |
+| 1 | the destination could not be written (e.g. `DEST` exists as a file) |
+| 2 | `ARCHIVE` does not exist, is unreadable, or is not a valid tar archive |
+| 3 | extraction would overwrite an existing file and `--overwrite` was not given |
+
+Usage errors (unknown command, missing argument) exit 2 via `argparse`.
+
+## Behaviour worth knowing
+
+- **Nothing is written when extraction would clobber.** Conflicts are detected
+  in a pass over the whole archive before the first byte is written, so a
+  failing extraction leaves the destination untouched rather than half-filled.
+- **With `--overwrite`**, existing regular files are replaced. A path that
+  exists as a *directory* where a file should go (or vice versa) is still an
+  error — removing a directory tree is too destructive to do implicitly.
+- **Members cannot escape `DEST`.** Absolute paths and paths containing `..`
+  are rejected (exit 2), and each target is re-checked against the real path of
+  `DEST` so that a pre-existing symlinked directory inside it cannot redirect a
+  write elsewhere. An existing symlink in the way of a file is removed rather
+  than written through.
+- **Symlink and special-file members are skipped** (they are listed, but not
+  extracted, and not counted): they are neither files nor directories, and
+  recreating a symlink is a path-escape hazard.
+- **Hard-link members are written as their own copy** of the linked member's
+  content, so no file in the archive goes missing. The extracted copies are
+  separate inodes rather than sharing one, which is the only difference from
+  GNU `tar` here.
+- File contents, relative paths, the executable bit and modification times are
+  preserved; ownership and the full permission mask are not.
+
+## Layout
+
+```
+src/tarx/__main__.py   entry point for `python -m tarx`
+src/tarx/cli.py        argument parsing, messages, exit statuses
+src/tarx/core.py       archive reading and extraction (no printing, no exits)
+tests/test_tarx.py     end-to-end tests driving the CLI as a subprocess
+```
+
+## Tests
+
+```
+PYTHONPATH=src python -m unittest discover -s tests
+```
+
+24 tests, passing on Python 3.11, 3.12 and 3.13.
